景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:3:每个参考题描述包含：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:4:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:5:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"221dfab4\" lines=\"6-19\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:11:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:12:Propagate a repeating striped pattern from a yellow border segment toward the opposite edge, recoloring foreground objects on certain stripes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:13:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:14:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:15:- bg = most common color. Foreground blobs of another color scattered in the interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:16:- A short yellow (4) segment sits on one border edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:17:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:18:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:19:- From the yellow segment, march toward the opposite edge in steps of 2 cells, cycling colors Y, Y, G (4, 4, 3). The 1-cell gap between stripes is forced to bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:20:- Yellow stripes paint only within the segment's span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:21:- Green stripes additionally recolor all non-bg pixels across the entire row/column to green.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:22:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:23:Key insight: Green stripes act as a \"flood\" that recolors existing objects on the full row/column, while yellow stripes are confined to the segment span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:24:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:25:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:26:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:27:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"7b0280bc\" lines=\"54-69\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:28:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:29:Recolor the shortest path between two terminal squares in a square-and-track graph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:30:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:31:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:32:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:33:- Two non-bg colors form solid NxN squares (N>=2): one color marks exactly 2 terminals, the other marks stations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:34:- A third non-bg color forms 1-cell-wide track segments connecting pairs of squares (graph edges).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:35:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:36:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:37:- Find the shortest path (fewest edges) between the two terminal squares.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:38:- Recolor every station square on that path to green.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:39:- Recolor every track segment along that path to grey.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:40:- Everything else unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:41:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:42:Key insight: The grid encodes a graph where squares are nodes and tracks are edges; the task is graph shortest-path, not spatial proximity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:43:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:44:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:45:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:46:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"458e3a53\" lines=\"19-32\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:47:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:48:Extract the compact table of solid cells hidden inside a separator lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:49:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:50:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:51:- The grid has full-width and full-height bars of one separator color, dividing it into rectangular cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:52:- Most cells contain a repeating multicolor pattern, while a contiguous rectangle of cells is solid monochrome.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:53:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:54:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:55:- Split the input into lattice cells using the full separator rows and columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:56:- Keep the cells whose full interior is one color, crop to their occupied rectangle, and output those colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:57:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:58:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:59:- The periodic pattern is noise; only completely solid lattice cells encode the reduced output grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:60:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:61:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:62:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:63:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2f767503\" lines=\"66-81\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:64:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:65:Erase each target-color object crossed by the ray pointed by the bar-and-control marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:66:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:67:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:68:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:69:- There is one three-pixel straight marker bar and one singleton control pixel adjacent to the bar center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:70:- The remaining non-background color forms multiple 4-connected target objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:71:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:72:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:73:- Cast a straight ray from the marker bar center in the direction away from the adjacent control pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:74:- Find every 4-connected target-color object that intersects that ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:75:- Recolor all pixels of those hit target objects to the background; all other pixels stay unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:76:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:77:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:78:- The whole object is erased when the center ray touches any of its pixels; the full marker bar width is not swept.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:79:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:80:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:81:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:82:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d6e50e54\" lines=\"8-25\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:83:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:84:Move each maroon marker toward the blue rectangle and recolor the rectangle red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:85:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:86:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:87:A background canvas contains one solid blue rectangular object and several isolated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:88:maroon marker pixels. Each marker is horizontally or vertically aligned with the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:89:rectangle and lies outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:90:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:91:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:92:Start with a background canvas, repaint the blue rectangle red, and move each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:93:maroon marker straight toward the rectangle along its row or column. Exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:94:marker is strictly closer to the rectangle than all others and enters the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:95:rectangle boundary; every other marker lands in the adjacent exterior cell just\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:96:outside its aligned side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:97:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:98:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:99:The single entering marker is the unique global nearest marker to the rectangle,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:100:not the nearest marker on each of the four sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:101:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:102:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:103:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:104:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d255d7a7\" lines=\"99-114\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:105:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:106:Move the patterned edge band to the opposite edge along every row or column whose band slice contains the trail color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:107:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:108:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:109:- The dominant color is the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:110:- The two foreground colors are a frequent trail color and a rarer marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:111:- All marker pixels lie nearest to one grid edge, and that edge contains trail-color runs that define the source-band thickness.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:112:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:113:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:114:- Choose the source edge identified by the marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:115:- A row or column perpendicular to that edge moves if its source-band slice contains the trail color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:116:- Copy that slice unchanged to the opposite edge, erase the remaining trail cells to background, and keep marker-only lines fixed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:117:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:118:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:119:- The marker color identifies the active edge, while the trail color identifies which parallel rows or columns carry an edge-band slice across the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:120:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:121:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:122:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:123:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"22806e14\" lines=\"23-37\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:124:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:125:Mark the center of each odd-sized solid square with the plus marker color, erasing the marker only when it is outside the marked-center field.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:126:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:127:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:128:- The dominant color is background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:129:- Exactly two foreground colors are present: one unique 3x3 plus marker and one color forming separated solid square objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:130:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:131:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:132:- For every non-marker 4-connected object, assert it is a solid square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:133:- If the square side length is odd, recolor its center pixel to the plus marker color; even-sided squares stay unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:134:- Preserve the plus marker when its center lies inside the bounding box of the odd-square centers; otherwise erase it to background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:135:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:136:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:137:- Odd-sided solid squares have a single visible center pixel, and the plus supplies the color used to identify those centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:138:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:139:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:140:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:141:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"7b80bb43\" lines=\"8-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:142:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:143:Remove diagonal staircase noise and complete broken straight lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:144:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:145:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:146:- bg = background; one foreground color fg forming axis-aligned lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:147:- Some fg pixels form 45° diagonal chains (8-connected but 4-disconnected from lines).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:148:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:149:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:150:- Delete all diagonal-only fg pixels (those with no orthogonal fg neighbor, only diagonal ones).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:151:- Fill short gaps in horizontal/vertical lines where a deleted diagonal was nearby.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:152:- Prune remaining diagonal-adjacent leaf pixels near former diagonal sites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:153:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:154:Key insight: Diagonal pixels are hints marking where a straight line is broken; their span sets the maximum gap size to fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:155:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:156:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:157:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:158:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2b83f449\" lines=\"10-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:159:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:160:Simulate tokens falling through a pipe network after gates rotate open.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:161:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:162:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:163:- Wall (0), bg (pipe fill), gate (horizontal 1×3 bars), token (small edge pixels).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:164:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:165:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:166:- Rotate each gate into a vertical blocker; gate cells become bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:167:- Tokens drop downward through bg, choosing the extreme column for their side (left→min, right→max).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:168:- Tokens settle at true pipe ends (adjacent to wall/boundary), packing inward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:169:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:170:Key insight: Tokens select drop columns by entry side and land at wall-bounded endpoints, ignoring blocker-bounded ones.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:171:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:172:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:173:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:174:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"bae5c565\" lines=\"10-28\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:175:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:176:Erase the top palette row and redraw it below as a widening wedge centered on its missing cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:177:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:178:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:179:- The top row is a palette row with exactly one background gap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:180:- Below it, the only foreground is one vertical marker bar of a single color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:181:- The marker bar is either in the gap column or immediately beside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:182:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:183:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:184:- Clear the grid to background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:185:- Starting at the top of the marker bar, each next row copies one more\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:186:  column of the top-row palette on both sides of the gap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:187:- Fill the gap column with the marker color, and keep the vertical marker bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:188:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:189:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:190:- The lone background cell in the top row is the center of the expanding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:191:  copy; the lower vertical bar provides the center color and the row where\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:192:  the expansion begins.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:193:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:194:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:195:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:196:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a09f6c25\" lines=\"33-50\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:197:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:198:Recolor each non-singleton red object by its symmetry axis and erase isolated red pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:199:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:200:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:201:- The grid has one dominant background color and red 4-connected foreground objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:202:- Every non-singleton red object has exactly one reflection symmetry category:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:203:  horizontal, vertical, or diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:204:- Single red pixels are noise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:205:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:206:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:207:- Start from an all-background output of the same shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:208:- Recolor horizontally symmetric red objects blue, vertically symmetric objects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:209:  green, and diagonally symmetric objects pink.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:210:- Leave isolated red pixels as background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:211:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:212:Key insight: The target color is not tied to object position or size; it is a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:213:label for the object's reflection symmetry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:214:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:215:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:216:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:217:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"5545f144\" lines=\"191-207\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:218:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:219:Move a triangular sprite across the grid, consuming aligned marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:220:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:221:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:222:- Frames concatenated horizontally with solid divider columns; bg is most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:223:- Each frame: a triangular arrow-shaped sprite and scattered single-pixel markers, all one color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:224:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:225:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:226:- Start from the rightmost frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:227:- At each step, exactly one cardinal direction from the head has reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:228:  markers (on a half-line: same row or column); the sprite advances to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:229:  nearest one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:230:- On reaching a marker, consume it; sprite re-faces that direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:231:- Repeat until no markers remain; output the final sprite position on a clean bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:232:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:233:Key insight: The triangle's tip encodes facing direction, which sets marker-consumption priority.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:234:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:235:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:236:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:237:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2e65ae53\" lines=\"88-103\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:238:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:239:Fill every lattice slot from the color assigned to that slot position by the other lattices.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:240:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:241:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:242:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:243:- The largest foreground color forms several one-pixel-thick rectangular lattice frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:244:- The frame lines divide each lattice into the same row-by-column set of rectangular slots; some slots already contain one non-frame color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:245:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:246:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:247:- Infer a color for each logical slot position from the colored slots across all lattice frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:248:- Repaint every slot interior in every lattice with the inferred color for its row/column position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:249:- Keep the frame lines and all background outside frames unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:250:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:251:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:252:- Slot sizes vary by frame, but the complete color pattern is indexed by lattice slot position rather than by absolute pixel size or location.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:253:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:254:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:255:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:256:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d6542281\" lines=\"72-91\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:257:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:258:Complete each partial marker mask by stamping the matching multicolor sprite over it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:259:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:260:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:261:- A dominant background contains one or more 8-connected multicolor sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:262:- Separate target masks use colors that already occur inside one of those sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:263:- A target mask may contain only one marker pixel or several same-alignment marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:264:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:265:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:266:- For each multicolor sprite, test every translation that aligns a target pixel with a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:267:  same-color sprite pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:268:- Keep the translations with maximal exact overlap against the existing target pixels,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:269:  rejecting translations that conflict with other foreground or overlap a source sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:270:- Stamp the whole sprite at those translations; if a non-marker sprite color occurs as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:271:  a single source pixel, consume that source-only marker back to background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:272:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:273:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:274:The scattered target pixels are partial copies: their same-color overlap with a sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:275:determines where the full sprite must be completed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:276:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:277:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:278:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:279:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"50c07299\" lines=\"8-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:280:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:281:Move the diagonal foreground segment to the next longer run along the same up-right diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:282:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:283:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:284:The grid has one background color and one foreground color. The foreground pixels form a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:285:contiguous one-pixel-wide segment on a single anti-diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:286:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:287:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:288:Erase the current segment. If its columns are c0..c1 and its length is L, draw the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:289:color on columns c1+1..c1+L+1 along the same anti-diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:290:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:291:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:292:The segment advances past its current upper-right end by one whole segment position, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:293:the next segment is one pixel longer than the current one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:294:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:295:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:296:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:297:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f8cc533f\" lines=\"10-25\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:298:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:299:Complete every colored sprite by applying the union of all aligned partial sprite masks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:300:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:301:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:302:- The dominant color is the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:303:- Each non-background color appears as a separated partial copy of one common sprite mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:304:- The copies share a top-left-aligned sprite window; some copies may be missing lower or right edge pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:305:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:306:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:307:- Crop each same-color mask to its bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:308:- Pad the crops to the maximum observed height and width, aligned at the top-left, and OR them into one complete template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:309:- Fill that template at every sprite location using the sprite's own color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:310:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:311:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:312:- No single input sprite is complete, but their missing cells are complementary, so the aligned union reveals the full mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:313:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:314:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:315:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:316:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"afe3afe9\" lines=\"106-119\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:317:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:318:Convert each hollow 3x3 symbol to one pixel and slide the pixels clockwise from the marked edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:319:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:320:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:321:- The grid has a background, one full-edge marker line, and monochrome hollow 3x3 foreground symbols.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:322:- The symbols lie on a coarse row/column lattice; fully empty lattice rows or columns are absent from the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:323:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:324:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:325:- Replace each hollow 3x3 symbol with one pixel of its color in the corresponding coarse-grid cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:326:- The marker edge gives the compaction direction by clockwise border travel: top -> right, right -> down, bottom -> left, left -> up.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:327:- Preserve the order of non-background pixels while sliding them as far as possible in that direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:328:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:329:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:330:- The large picture is a scaled symbolic grid, and the blue edge marker acts as a gravity direction rather than as output content.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:331:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:332:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:333:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:334:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9f41bd9c\" lines=\"10-30\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:335:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:336:Move the side-attached foreground object to the opposite wall, shear its lower rows inward, and paint the crossed floor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:337:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:338:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:339:- The top row is the upper background color and the bottom row is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:340:  floor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:341:- A single non-background, non-floor object touches exactly one vertical\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:342:  grid edge and rests immediately above the first solid floor row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:343:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:344:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:345:- Clear the source object to the upper background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:346:- Repaint each object row on the opposite side: the first three relative\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:347:  rows keep the edge alignment, and each lower row shifts one more pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:348:  inward from that side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:349:- On the first floor row, repaint the traversed side-to-object segment\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:350:  maroon, stopping just before the final outer bottom support pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:351:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:352:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:353:- The side of the source object gives the horizontal direction, while the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:354:  row index inside the object gives the one-cell-per-row diagonal shear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:355:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:356:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:357:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:358:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ff2825db\" lines=\"18-36\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:359:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:360:Select the majority interior marker color, then redraw the framed board as that color's frame plus its bounding-box outline.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:361:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:362:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:363:- The top row is a copied palette made from adjacent equal color pairs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:364:- Below it is a one-cell-thick rectangular frame around a black interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:365:- Non-black, non-frame interior pixels are marker colors; one marker color has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:366:  the unique highest count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:367:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:368:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:369:- Keep the palette row unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:370:- Pick the uniquely most frequent interior marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:371:- Clear the lower board to black, recolor its outer frame with the picked color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:372:  and draw the picked color's interior bounding-box border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:373:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:374:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:375:- The noisy marker cloud is not preserved as pixels; only the majority marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:376:  color and its spatial extent define the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:377:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:378:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:379:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:380:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"18286ef8\" lines=\"17-31\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:381:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:382:Use the pink control pixel to choose where the maroon pixel belongs inside the grey 3x3 region, and turn the control pixel maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:383:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:384:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:385:- The grid contains one 3x3 region made from eight grey pixels and one maroon pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:386:- There is exactly one pink control pixel outside that region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:387:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:388:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:389:- Restore the old maroon cell in the 3x3 region to grey.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:390:- Compare the pink pixel to the 3x3 region: above/same band/below selects top/middle/bottom, and left/same band/right selects left/middle/right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:391:- Paint the selected cell maroon and recolor the pink control pixel maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:392:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:393:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:394:- The pink pixel acts as a relative-position marker for a 3x3 target inside the grey region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:395:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:396:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:397:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:398:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:399:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:400:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:401:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:402:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:403:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:404:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:405:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:406:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:407:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:408:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:409:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:410:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:411:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:412:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:413:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:414:请一次性生成5个`<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:415:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:416:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:417:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:418:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:419:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:420:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算（取模） / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:421:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:422:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:423:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:424:6. 新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:425:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:426:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:427:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:428:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.md:429:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5/prompt.m